 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Finite direct sums",
 "statement": "Finite direct sums of finite locally constant sheaves are finite locally\nconstant; the same holds for locally constant sheaves and for finite\nsheaves.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-properbasechange/lemma-constructible-flc-biproduct.md",
  "place": "node lemma-constructible-flc-biproduct, order 1295"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-constructible-constant",
  "def-constructible-finite",
  "def-constructible-finite-locally-constant",
  "def-constructible-locally-constant",
  "def-kun-separably-closed"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "For two sheaves with trivialising data $(U_i\\to X)_i$ and $(V_j\\to X)_j$,\nthe family $(U_i\\times_XV_j\\to X)_{i,j}$ is an étale cover trivialising\nboth. Restriction to a localised site is exact and preserves finite direct\nsums, and a finite direct sum $M_X\\oplus N_X$ of constant sheaves is the\nconstant sheaf $(M\\oplus N)_X$, because sheafification and the constant\npresheaf functor are additive. Stalks commute with finite direct sums,\nand a finite direct sum of finite sets is finite.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
